<!-- ClickHouse's date parsing on insert kept as 26.2 has it, in the default
     profile (workplan 0119 §3 item 9, option 2, the owner's decision of
     2026-11-02: 26.8.36.3-lts, ahead of the 26.2.19.43 Trigger.dev v4.8.3
     pins). Read at v26.8.34.13-lts (src/Core/SettingsChangesHistory.cpp).

     date_time_input_format and cast_string_to_date_time_mode = basic. Both
     are best_effort from 26.5. Under it a JSON string such as
     2024-11-06T20:37:00.123Z, in a path of a JSON column that declares no
     type, is inferred and stored as a DateTime64(9), where 26.2 stores a
     String (tryInferDateTime64 in src/Formats/SchemaInferenceUtils.cpp
     follows date_time_input_format). Here that reaches metrics_v1.attributes
     (Trigger.dev v4.8.3's migration 019), where task metrics are written.

     input_format_read_datetime_number_as_raw_value = 1. From 26.8 it is
     false, under which a bare number fed to a DateTime64 column in JSON is
     read as seconds. Trigger.dev's run, session and webhook replication sends
     milliseconds into DateTime64(3) columns (internal-packages/clickhouse/
     src/taskRuns.ts at v4.8.3). Replication is off here
     (RUN_REPLICATION_ENABLED unset), so this guards a switch, not a running
     write. The setting does not exist at 26.2: this file travels with the
     pin too.

     In users.d, since profile settings in config.d are not read as profile
     settings. Mounted as this one file, never the directory: the image's
     entrypoint writes users.d/default-user.xml at every start, under
     `set -e`, and Trigger.dev's own compose mounts one file there the same
     way (hosting/docker/webapp/docker-compose.yml at v4.8.3). Nothing else
     belongs here: the four profile settings in clickhouse-override.xml do
     nothing from config.d, as on 26.2, and moving them would switch them on,
     a change of its own.

     docs/managed-bring-up.md, "Moving ClickHouse", has the check that all
     three are in force. -->
<clickhouse>
    <profiles>
        <default>
            <date_time_input_format>basic</date_time_input_format>
            <cast_string_to_date_time_mode>basic</cast_string_to_date_time_mode>
            <input_format_read_datetime_number_as_raw_value>1</input_format_read_datetime_number_as_raw_value>
        </default>
    </profiles>
</clickhouse>
